---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL } from "../lib/site";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Terms of Use" }];
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="HomeDIYCalc terms of use: the calculators are free estimates for planning purposes, provided without warranty, by an individual operator based in Malaysia."
  canonical="/terms-of-use/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: November 23, 2026.</p>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-slate-700">
    <p>
      By using HomeDIYCalc, you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not
      use the site.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. The service</h2>
    <p>
      HomeDIYCalc provides free online calculators for home improvement material
      estimates. The service is provided free of charge, with no account or registration.
      The site is operated independently by an individual based in Malaysia; it is not
      operated by a company.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. Estimates, not advice</h2>
    <p>
      All calculator results are estimates for planning purposes. They are not
      professional, engineering, or construction advice. Results depend on the accuracy of
      the measurements and values you enter, and on site conditions the calculators cannot
      see. Always confirm quantities with your supplier and, for structural or safety-critical
      work, with a qualified professional. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the calculators for personal and commercial project planning. You may
      not use the site to mislead others, to scrape the site at a rate that degrades it
      for other users, or to attempt to interfere with its operation.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. No warranty</h2>
    <p>
      The site and its calculators are provided “as is” and “as available”, without
      warranties of any kind, express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, fitness
      for a particular purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that results will be
      error-free or that the site will be uninterrupted.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">5. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, HomeDIYCalc is not liable for any loss,
      damage, or cost arising from use of the site or reliance on its estimates,
      including over- or under-ordering of materials.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">6. Your data</h2>
    <p>
      The site does not ask for your personal information. Calculator inputs are
      processed in your browser and are not sent anywhere; anything you save with My
      Project is stored only in your own browser. If you email us, we receive your
      email address and message and use them only to answer you. Our hosting provider
      processes standard request data to serve and protect the site. See the
      <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">7. Operator and governing law</h2>
    <p>
      HomeDIYCalc is operated by an individual based in Malaysia. These terms are
      governed by the laws of Malaysia.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">8. Copyright</h2>
    <p>
      © 2026 HomeDIYCalc. All rights reserved. The original text, design, and calculator
      pages of this website are the operator's own work; you may use the site for
      your own project planning, but you may not copy or republish its content as your
      own. Third-party materials and open-source dependencies used on the site remain
      the property of their owners and are used under their respective licenses; this
      reservation of rights does not change those licenses. The website's source code
      is published in a public GitHub repository and is not licensed under an
      open-source license; no permission to reuse the code is granted here.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">9. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      You can reach the operator by email at{" "}
      <a href={`mailto:${SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="underline">{SITE_CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      See the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">10. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may be updated from time to time. Continued use of the site after an
      update constitutes acceptance of the updated terms.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
